1. Project Overview
Project Name: FitBuddy-AI
Type: AI-powered fitness plan generator
AI Technology: Google Gemini models
Primary Goal: Generate personalized workout plans based on individual user requirements.

Problem
Users often receive generic workout routines that don't consider their fitness goals, experience, available equipment, schedule, or preferred workout duration.

Proposed Solution
FitBuddy-AI collects user information and uses Gemini to generate a structured, personalized workout plan that can be displayed and tracked through the application.

2. Stakeholders
Stakeholder	Role
User	Provides fitness information and follows the generated plan
Administrator	Manages users and application data
Developer	Develops and maintains the system
Gemini API	Generates personalized fitness content
Database	Stores user profiles, plans, and progress

3. Functional Requirements
FR1 — User Registration
The system shall allow users to:

Create an account

Log in and log out

Manage their profile

FR2 — Fitness Assessment
The system shall collect relevant information such as:

Age

Height and weight

Fitness experience

Fitness goal

Available equipment

Number of workout days

Preferred workout duration

Workout preferences

FR3 — Goal Selection
Users should be able to select goals such as:

Weight management

Muscle development

Strength development

General fitness

Endurance

FR4 — AI Workout Generation
The system shall send the user's profile and requirements to Gemini and generate a personalized workout plan.

The generated plan should contain:

Workout days

Target muscle groups/focus

Exercises

Sets

Repetitions

Rest periods

Estimated workout duration

Warm-up

Cooldown

Progression guidance

FR5 — Workout Display
The generated plan shall be presented through an easy-to-understand dashboard.

Example:

Monday
────────────────────
Chest + Triceps

Push-ups
3 × 10-15
Rest: 60 sec

Dumbbell Press
3 × 8-12
Rest: 90 sec

[Start Workout]

FR6 — Exercise Substitution
Users should be able to request an alternative when they cannot perform an exercise.

Example:

Dumbbell Squat
      ↓
"Replace this exercise"
      ↓
Alternative exercise

FR7 — Workout Tracking
The system shall allow users to:

Start a workout

Mark exercises as completed

Record sets/repetitions where appropriate

Mark the overall workout as completed

FR8 — Progress Tracking
The application shall maintain information such as:

Completed workouts

Weekly activity

Workout history

Personal progress metrics

FR9 — AI Adaptation
Based on appropriate user feedback, FitBuddy-AI should be able to generate an adjusted workout.

Example:

"Today's workout needs to be 25 minutes."

The system can generate a shorter version while maintaining the overall training objective.

FR10 — AI Fitness Assistant
Users should eventually be able to ask natural-language questions such as:

"What can I do instead of lunges?"

"I only have resistance bands today."

The Gemini-powered assistant can provide relevant alternatives and explanations.

4. Non-Functional Requirements
Performance
Workout plans should be generated within a reasonable response time.

The UI should remain responsive while Gemini is processing.

Usability
Simple onboarding

Mobile-friendly interface

Clear exercise instructions

Easy-to-read workout cards

Minimal steps to start a workout

Security
Protect user accounts and authentication information.

Store API credentials securely on the server.

Do not expose the Gemini API key in client-side code.

Protect personal user data.

Reliability
Handle Gemini API failures gracefully.

Validate generated JSON before displaying it.

Provide a fallback message when a plan cannot be generated.

Scalability
The architecture should allow additional users and AI features without requiring a complete redesign.

Maintainability
Use modular components for:

Authentication

User profiles

Gemini integration

Workout generation

Workout tracking

Progress tracking

5. AI Requirements
Gemini should generate structured output rather than unrestricted text.

For example:

{
  "planName": "Beginner Fitness Plan",
  "durationWeeks": 4,
  "workouts": [
    {
      "day": "Monday",
      "focus": "Full Body",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "name": "Bodyweight Squat",
          "sets": 3,
          "reps": "10-15",
          "restSeconds": 60
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Gemini's structured-output functionality can be used to make generated responses conform to a predefined schema.

The application should validate the generated data before presenting it to the user.

6. Safety Requirements
Because FitBuddy-AI deals with fitness, safety needs to be part of the requirements.

The system should:

Avoid presenting itself as a medical professional.

Avoid diagnosing injuries or medical conditions.

Encourage users to seek qualified professional advice for relevant medical or injury concerns.

Include appropriate exercise-safety guidance.

Allow users to report an exercise as unsuitable.

Avoid making unsupported medical claims.

